    "interpretation": "Most sampled word exchanges require two GPI reads in each ACK phase. high/low_wait_words count more than one read, so a large wait_words value mostly reflects the ordinary handshake and does not by itself identify FIFO saturation. Event 768 has prolonged ACK-low wait (72-read maximum), while nearby unsampled chunks also transfer slowly. The samples demonstrate actual extra low-phase polling but do not identify all stall locations or directly time wait phases."
  },
