  "supported_conclusion": "Synchronous host-to-FPGA transfer dominates measured polling time, not helper pipe reads or time outside the media poll. Common per-word handshake/bridge cost is a substantial throughput floor, with occasional longer ACK-low waits. At ~1.43 MB/s the supply remains below the fixture average ~2.33 MB/s. Variable encoded picture sizes remain consistent with alternating smooth and slow passages.",
  "source_review": {
    "baseline_main_commit": "0a8fb44ccec6d69c8b7f158abd5fe8065ab2bf4f",
    "reviewed_paths": [
      "host/main_mister/0001-mediaplayer-arm-loader.patch",
      "Main_MiSTer/fpga_io.cpp:688",
      "MediaPlayer_top_00.svh:148",
      "sys/hps_io.sv:191",
      "sys/sys_top.v:259"
    ],
    "finding": "Ordinary fpga_spi uses three GPO writes plus both ACK polling phases per word. FPGA ACK progression is gated by io_wait/vs_wait except the initial strobe capture; ioctl_wait carries input FIFO full. An unchecked fast-block substitution would discard this protection. Samples support optimizing the transfer path, not assuming FIFO waits never occur."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "One run per condition; near-identical aggregate cadence is not a controlled estimate of instrumentation overhead.",
    "Sampled full chunks have a higher median transfer cost than unsampled chunks, but are not paired measurements of the same transfer.",
